  "term": "reserpine",
  "definition": "Reserpine is an alkaloid from Rauwolfia plant roots that reduces stored norepinephrine, other catecholamines, and serotonin in nerve terminals. It has been used as a blood pressure drug, an antipsychotic, and a research substance, but side effects have limited its clinical use.",
